---
components: ["LocaleProvider"]
description: LocaleProvider sets the locale, time zone, hour cycle, week start and text direction once, for every component below it that formats a value.
---

<script>
  import {
    DataTable,
    DatePicker,
    DatePickerInput,
    FileUploader,
    LocaleProvider,
    NumberInput,
    Pagination,
    RelativeTime,
    Select,
    SelectItem,
    Stack,
  } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  const locales = [
    { id: "en-US", text: "English (United States)" },
    { id: "de-DE", text: "Deutsch (Deutschland)" },
    { id: "ar-EG", text: "العربية (مصر)" },
    { id: "ja-JP", text: "日本語 (日本)" },
    { id: "fr-CH", text: "Français (Suisse)" },
  ];

  const now = Date.parse("2026-09-13T12:00:00Z");
  const file = new File(["x".repeat(1500)], "report.txt");
  const headers = [{ key: "name", value: "Name" }];
  const rows = [
    { id: "a", name: "Zoë" },
    { id: "b", name: "Ärger" },
    { id: "c", name: "Anna" },
    { id: "d", name: "Östen" },
  ];

  let locale = "de-DE";
</script>

## Basic

Wrap the part of an app that formats values in `LocaleProvider` and set `locale` to a BCP 47 language tag. Every component below that formats a number, a date, a time or a sort order uses it, and each one updates when `locale` changes.

Set `dir="auto"` to also set the writing direction from the locale: right to left for Arabic and Hebrew, left to right for the rest. The content then renders in an element with that `dir` and a `lang`.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <Select labelText="Locale" bind:selected={locale}>
    {#each locales as { id, text } (id)}
      <SelectItem value={id} {text} />
    {/each}
  </Select>
  <LocaleProvider {locale} timeZone="UTC" dir="auto">
    <Stack gap={6}>
      <NumberInput labelText="Amount" value={1234567.89} />
      <RelativeTime date={now - 5 * 60 * 1000} {now} />
      <DatePicker datePickerType="single">
        <DatePickerInput labelText="Date" placeholder="mm/dd/yyyy" />
      </DatePicker>
      <Pagination totalItems={12345} pageSize={10} pageSizes={[10]} />
      <DataTable
        sortable
        sortKey="name"
        sortDirection="ascending"
        {headers}
        {rows}
      />
      <FileUploader labelTitle="Files" files={[file]} fileSize />
    </Stack>
  </LocaleProvider>
</Stack>

## Precedence

A component reads its own prop first, then the nearest `LocaleProvider`, then its own default. Without a provider nothing changes: each component keeps the default it has today, whether that is `"en"`, the runtime's locale or no formatting at all.

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Set `locale` on a component that must differ from the rest | The prop wins over the provider, so one date can stay in ISO order. |
| Leave `locale` unset on the rest | They follow the provider, including when it changes at runtime. |
| Set `locale` on the provider | The tag is never read from the browser, so a server and a browser that set it print the same text. |

Only the fields a provider sets take effect. A field it leaves unset comes from the provider above it, and from the component's default when there is none.

## Number formatting

`NumberInput`, `Pagination` and `FileUploader` write numbers with the locale's digits and separators. The `numberingSystem` of a provider swaps the digits only, such as Western digits in an Arabic locale.

A `NumberInput` with a locale from a provider is a text field with `inputmode="decimal"`, as it is with its own `locale`, so it parses what a person types in that locale.

<Stack gap={6}>
  <LocaleProvider locale="ar-EG" dir="auto">
    <NumberInput labelText="المبلغ" value={1234567.89} />
  </LocaleProvider>
  <LocaleProvider locale="ar-EG" numberingSystem="latn" dir="auto">
    <NumberInput labelText="المبلغ" value={1234567.89} />
  </LocaleProvider>
</Stack>

## Dates and times

Set `timeZone` to an IANA zone, such as `"Europe/Zurich"`, so a time prints in that zone and not in the browser's. Set `hourCycle` to `"h23"` for a 24-hour clock or `"h12"` for a 12-hour one. Set `weekStart` from `0` (Sunday) to `6` (Saturday) for the first day of the week in a calendar, and `calendar` for a calendar such as `"buddhist"`.

`hourCycle`, `numberingSystem` and `calendar` are written into the locale tag as Unicode extension keys, so every `Intl` formatter honors them. They need a `locale`.

Hover the time to read the absolute time in the provider's zone and hour cycle.

<LocaleProvider locale="en-US" timeZone="Asia/Tokyo" hourCycle="h23">
  <RelativeTime date={now - 5 * 60 * 1000} {now} />
</LocaleProvider>

A `DatePicker` takes `weekStart` too. Here the week starts on Monday in an English calendar.

<LocaleProvider locale="en-US" weekStart={1}>
  <DatePicker datePickerType="single">
    <DatePickerInput labelText="Date" placeholder="mm/dd/yyyy" />
  </DatePicker>
</LocaleProvider>

## Sorting

`DataTable` orders strings with the collation of the locale. In Swedish "ä" sorts after "z", and in German it sorts with "a". A `sort` function on the table or on a header takes precedence.

<LocaleProvider locale="sv">
  <DataTable
    sortable
    sortKey="name"
    sortDirection="ascending"
    {headers}
    {rows}
  />
</LocaleProvider>

## Nesting

Providers nest. An inner one overrides the fields it sets and keeps the rest, so an inner provider that sets only `locale` keeps the `timeZone` above it.

<LocaleProvider locale="de-CH">
  <Stack gap={6}>
    <NumberInput labelText="Betrag (de-CH)" value={1234567.89} />
    <LocaleProvider locale="fr-CH">
      <NumberInput labelText="Montant (fr-CH)" value={1234567.89} />
    </LocaleProvider>
  </Stack>
</LocaleProvider>

## Direction

`dir` takes `"ltr"`, `"rtl"` or `"auto"`. `"auto"` reads the direction from the locale with `Intl.Locale`, and from the script of the locale's likely subtags where the browser has no text info. A provider with `dir` renders an element that carries `dir` and `lang`, and components inside read the direction as they do in a [LayoutDirection](/components/LayoutDirection). Use `tag` to render another element. A provider without `dir` renders no element.

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Set `dir="auto"` on a provider that wraps one part of a page | The part follows its locale, such as an Arabic form in an English app. |
| Write `<html lang dir>` for a whole app, with `getLocaleDirection(locale)` | The first paint is mirrored and the markup is the same on the server and in the browser. |
| Nest a provider with `dir="ltr"` for code or identifiers | The nearest direction wins. |

A provider does not change `<html>`. It cannot on the server, and two providers would overwrite each other.

```svelte
<!-- src/hooks.server.js -->
<script module>
  import { getLocaleDirection } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  export const handle = ({ event, resolve }) => {
    const locale = event.cookies.get("locale") ?? "en-US";
    return resolve(event, {
      transformPageChunk: ({ html }) =>
        html
          .replace("%lang%", locale)
          .replace("%dir%", getLocaleDirection(locale)),
    });
  };
</script>
```

See the [right-to-left guide](/right-to-left) for what flips and what stays left to right.

## Server rendering

A server and a browser that format with different defaults print different text, and Svelte replaces the text when it hydrates. `RelativeTime` and `Pagination` do this today when the server's locale or time zone is not the browser's.

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Set `locale` and `timeZone` on the provider on the server and in the browser | Neither is read from the runtime, so the markup matches. |
| Read the locale from the request, such as a cookie or `Accept-Language`, and send it to the client | The server has no `navigator.language`. |
| Keep the provider in the root layout | Every component reads the same values, and a route change keeps them. |
| Pass `now` to a `RelativeTime` until the page is mounted | Its text depends on the clock, so a prerendered page is stale at once. |
| Do not use formatted text as an `id` or a `key` | Browsers disagree on some strings, such as `1'234.50 CHF` and `CHF 1'234.50`. |

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script>
  import { LocaleProvider } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  export let data;
</script>

<LocaleProvider
  locale={data.locale}
  timeZone={data.timeZone}
  dir="auto"
>
  <slot />
</LocaleProvider>
```

## Translated text

`translate` sets the translation function that components with a `translateWithId` prop read, the one `setTranslateContext` sets. Return `undefined` for an id to keep the English text. A nested provider's function is asked first.

```svelte
<LocaleProvider locale="de-DE" translate={(id) => messages[id]}>
  <NumberInput labelText="Menge" />
</LocaleProvider>
```

The text props, such as `Pagination`'s `itemsPerPageText`, are not covered: pass those on the component. `Pagination`'s text functions receive a `format` argument that writes a number in the locale, so a translated sentence keeps the locale's digits.

```svelte
<Pagination
  totalItems={12345}
  itemRangeText={(min, max, total, format) =>
    `${format(min)}–${format(max)} von ${format(total)} Elementen`}
/>
```

## Reading the context

Call `getLocaleContext` during component initialization to read the nearest provider in your own components. It returns a store that holds the merged settings, and an empty object outside a provider.

```svelte
<script>
  import { getLocaleContext } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  export let date;
  export let locale = undefined;

  const context = getLocaleContext();

  $: formatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale ?? $context.locale, {
    dateStyle: "medium",
    timeZone: $context.timeZone,
  });
</script>

{formatter.format(date)}
```

`$context.locale` is the tag with `hourCycle`, `numberingSystem` and `calendar` applied, such as `de-CH-u-nu-arab`. `$context.baseLocale` is the tag as it was set.

## Components that read it

| Component | Reads |
| :--- | :--- |
| NumberInput | `locale` |
| RelativeTime | `locale`, `timeZone` |
| Pagination | `locale`, for the numbers in its default text |
| DataTable | `locale`, for sorting |
| FileUploader | `locale`, for file sizes |
| DatePicker, DateCalendar | `locale`, `weekStart` |

The other components that take a `locale` prop, such as `BigNumber`, `Meter` and `MultiSelect`, do not read the provider yet.
